e of Discrete Random Variables"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ab2a799f-1de3-5949-9d28-e92b9b2c1853" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159531} {:answer/id #uuid "bf333e3f-1e9a-512c-9ee9-c815a6ddb929" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159532} {:answer/id #uuid "e0b5d122-7f9e-5765-8d55-ba39fdfa2b52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159533} {:answer/id #uuid "4536fe93-9e65-5770-ab9c-9ff6f05a6008" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159534} {:answer/id #uuid "52fc1410-4377-5834-a089-600330682922" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the statements are true." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159535}] :answer-field/id #uuid "20cfccdf-0f62-55e2-92b1-68319ea00399" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159530}] :question/id #uuid "1e60a4ff-2b15-51cb-bace-fa72d363609f" :question/math-academy-id "q-143438" :question/problem "The joint probability distribution $f(x, y)$ of the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given below.\n\n| $f$ | $Y = 0$ | $Y = 1$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| $X = 0$ | $0.05$ | $0.15$ |\n| $X = 1$ | $0.25$ | $0.55$ |\n\nWhich of the following statements is true?\n\n1. $P(X = 0, Y = 1) = P(X = 0) \\cdot P(Y = 1)$\n2. $P(X = x, Y = y) = P(X = x) \\cdot P(Y = y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$\n3. $X$ and $Y$ are independent\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question." :question/requires-calculator true}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162458 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 1759218616215