$$0.8$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $P(X = 1, Y = 1) = P(X = 1) \\cdot P(Y = 1)$\n2. $P(X = x, Y = y) = P(X = x) \\cdot P(Y = y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$\n3. $X$ and $Y$ are independent\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question." :question/requires-calculator true}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162468 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161919 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "559e653a-2ab9-54a8-84e3-02bf106a8f47" :knowledge-point/title "Inferring Divisibility in Algebraic Expressions" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048604 :topic/math-academy-id 3080 :topic/title "Integer Divisibility"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82d1da03-9afc-57f1-aa22-7ec29f4d6115" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160017} {:answer/id #uuid "0f706fdd-d228-5926-8f09-8f20f84b6cfe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160018} {:answer/id #uuid "162c28ec-91a6-5219-ada7-6abadc884429" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160019} {:answer/id #uuid "3f9afa41-cee5-5ccd-aaa1-46ee696cc7a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160020} {:answer/id #uuid "44989f39-2eb5-5626-8c4c-23334d26dfef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160021}] :answer-field/id #uuid "65dc1b56-5de7-5f54-b36a-f0ab0d0437ab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160016}] :question/id #uuid "12ebf358-031f-5a56-a47f-c0acf763bd6e" :question/math-academy-id "q-221922" :qu